CASES=[dict(slug='long-distance-water-tunnel-inspection',title='Long-distance water-tunnel inspection in China',model='AD-400',type='TUNNEL INSPECTION',source='The supplied manufacturer brochure describes an AD-400 long-distance headrace water-tunnel inspection project associated with China Southern Power Grid.',task='Access a flooded water tunnel for inspection and data collection over a long route.',system='AD-400 vehicle, external tethered supply and a project-specific inspection package. The final sensors, tether management and position reference need to be checked against the original project record.',review=['Actual inspected route length and the vehicle version','Tunnel bends, flow, access and deployment conditions','Position referencing, coverage and data-quality criteria','Original footage, logs, recovery plan and acceptance record'],boundary='The available summary does not establish universal range, localization accuracy or suitability for every tunnel. Performance and transfer to a new site require the underlying project records.',sol='underwater-tunnel-inspection',product='ad-400-tunnel-inspection-rov',img=PRODUCTS[2],reported='For this development project, the manufacturer reports inspection inside a 5.5 km headrace tunnel, including 360-degree coverage, long-distance power and communication, and cruising capability. This is the brochure’s project statement, distinct from the 5 km maximum range on the current product webpage. The manufacturer reports delivery to China Southern Power Grid’s energy-storage company in August 2023 and a 40% shorter single-inspection cycle.'),dict(slug='underwater-trash-rack-cleaning',title='Underwater intake trash-rack cleaning in China',model='A-80',type='SUBMERGED CLEANING',source='The supplied manufacturer brochure identifies an A-80 application at the Baihetan hydropower intake trash rack in China.',task='Assess and clean suitable submerged intake surfaces using a remotely operated contact-cleaning platform.',system='A-80 vehicle and its cleaning attachment with external support equipment. Verify the pump, hose, attachment and actual substrate from the original project materials.',review=['Rack spacing, angle, material and deposit type','Cleaning attachment and pump/hose configuration','Before-and-after evidence under comparable conditions','Measured area, working time and substrate condition'],boundary='This reference does not demonstrate extraction of every type of large debris or a universal cleaning rate. Request the original operating record and a representative surface test.',sol='underwater-trash-rack-cleaning',product='a-80-cleaning-robot',img=PRODUCTS[3],reported='For this project, the manufacturer reports wall-adhering travel and cavitation water-jet cleaning, without draining the water, stopping the facility or sending personnel underwater. These are project-specific manufacturer statements, not promises for every intake.'),dict(slug='hydropower-dam-crawler-inspection',title='Dual-mode crawler inspection of hydropower structures in China',model='A-400',type='HYDROPOWER INSPECTION',source='The supplied manufacturer brochure describes the development of a dual-mode (swimming and crawling) underwater inspection robot for China Yangtze Power, for inspection of submerged hydropower structures.',task='Reach submerged dam and hydropower structures through flowing water, hold position on the surface and record defects for assessment.',system='A-400 dual-mode vehicle with cameras, positioning and protective systems as described by the manufacturer. The supplied sensors, adhesion method and data outputs need to be checked against the original project record.',review=['Structure type, surface material and fouling condition','Flow conditions at the inspected surface during operation','Defect types detected, positioning method and data samples','Launch and recovery arrangement, operating time and acceptance record'],boundary='The available summary does not establish performance limits, defect-recognition accuracy or suitability for every dam or intake. Transfer to a new site requires the underlying project records and a site review.',sol='industrial-underwater-inspection',product='a-400-crawler-inspection-robot',img=next(p for p in PRODUCTS if p['id']=='a-400'),reported='For this development project, the manufacturer reports switching from a swimming approach to stable crawling on the structure surface, and high-definition inspection and assessment of submerged structures. These are manufacturer statements about a development project, not guaranteed specifications. The manufacturer’s timeline: purchase contract in September 2021, delivery in June 2022, and in-water testing with operator training in July 2022.'),dict(slug='fishing-port-surface-cleaning',title='Autonomous surface cleaning at a fishing port in China',model='S-Cleaner',type='SURFACE CLEANING',source='The supplied manufacturer brochure describes routine surface cleaning by an S-Cleaner vessel at the Yazhou central fishing port in Sanya, China.',task='Replace intermittent manual and mechanical collection of floating debris in a working fishing port with continuous, unmanned cleaning.',system='S-Cleaner vessel with autonomous cruising and debris recognition. The docking, charging and unloading arrangement and the route plan need to be checked against the original operating record.',review=['Port layout, vessel traffic and wind and wave exposure','Debris types, daily volume and unloading arrangement','Operating hours, interventions and downtime','Measured area, collected weight and weighing method'],boundary='The reported figures describe one port over a defined period. They do not establish a universal coverage rate or performance in exposed or busy waters. Request the operating log and run a site trial.',sol='water-surface-cleaning',product='s-cleaner-surface-cleaning-vessel',img=next(p for p in PRODUCTS if p['id']=='s-cleaner'),reported='The manufacturer reports that, by November 2025, the vessel had worked routinely in the port for more than 91 days, covering about 200,000 m² of water and collecting 3,829 kg of floating marine debris. These are manufacturer-reported operating figures.')]
def case_card(c):
 return f'<article class="case-card"><div class="case-image">{img(c["img"])}</div><div class="case-copy"><span class="eyebrow">CHINA / MANUFACTURER REFERENCE</span><h3>{link("/case-studies/"+c["slug"]+"/",c["title"])}</h3><p>{c["task"]}</p>{link("/case-studies/"+c["slug"]+"/","Read project context","text-link")}</div></article>'
write('/case-studies/','Underwater Robotics Manufacturer Case Studies','Manufacturer project references from China for long-distance tunnel inspection, underwater intake cleaning, hydropower crawler inspection and fishing-port surface cleaning.',intro('MANUFACTURER PROJECT REFERENCES','Evidence needs context.','Explore the tasks described in Boya Gongdao’s supplied brochure, then request the underlying records relevant to your site.')+'<section class="wrap section"><div class="note">These are manufacturer references from China. They are not overseas deliveries or projects performed by '+B+'. Product images illustrate the equipment; they are not site photographs.</div><div class="case-grid">'+''.join(case_card(c) for c in CASES)+'</div></section>'+cta())
for c in CASES:
 body=intro('CHINA / '+c['type'],c['title'],'Manufacturer project reference • Equipment: '+c['model'])
 reported=c['reported']
 body+=f'<section class="wrap section article-grid"><aside class="article-aside">{img(c["img"])}<p class="meta">Product image, not a project photograph.</p><h3>Project attribution</h3><p>Source: supplied Boya Gongdao brochure. Implementation is attributed to the manufacturer.</p>{link("/equipment/"+c['product']+'/',"Review "+c['model'],"text-link")}</aside><div class="article-body"><section><h2>The published reference</h2><p>{c["source"]}</p></section><section><h2>The task</h2><p>{c["task"]}</p></section><section><h2>The system to verify</h2><p>{c["system"]}</p></section><section><h2>The reported outcome</h2><p>{reported}</p></section><section>{section_list("Evidence for a comparable project",c["review"])}</section><section><h2>What this reference establishes</h2><p>The brochure identifies a relevant manufacturer application. It offers a starting point for asking about the technical approach and original evidence.</p><p>{c["boundary"]}</p>{link("/solutions/"+c['sol']+'/',"Read the application guide","text-link")}</section></div></section>'+cta('Assess a similar task.','Use your site geometry and operating conditions to review whether the referenced approach is transferable.')
 write('/case-studies/'+c['slug']+'/',c['title'],c['source'],body)

support=intro('TRAINING / SPARES / TECHNICAL COORDINATION','Plan support before deployment.','Define who supports the operator, how faults are diagnosed and what happens if equipment needs repair.')
support+='<section class="wrap section"><div class="steps">'+''.join(f'<article><span>0{i}</span><h3>{t}</h3><p>{d}</p></article>' for i,t,d in [(1,'Operator preparation','Confirm training scope, operator competence, checks, launch and recovery procedures.'),(2,'Remote diagnosis','Collect vehicle identity, software version, symptoms, logs, photos and relevant operating conditions.'),(3,'Manufacturer escalation','Identify the technical contact and the evidence needed to assess the fault or approve a remedy.'),(4,'Parts or repair','Agree the replacement part, repair location, shipping responsibilities and return-to-service test.')])+'</div></section>'
support+='<section class="section band"><div class="wrap two-col"><div><h2>Make responsibilities explicit.</h2><p>The quotation and purchase agreement should identify the seller, warranty provider and support contact. Local servicing, field attendance and repair turnaround depend on an agreed arrangement.</p><p>No overseas service-center network or guaranteed response time is represented on this site.</p></div><div>'+section_list('Agree before purchase',['Warranty scope, exclusions and claim process','Support languages and working hours','Recommended spares and consumables','Remote support, training and on-site options','Repair location, shipping, duties and costs','Software updates and documentation'])+'</div></div></section>'
support+='<section class="wrap section"><p class="eyebrow">REQUESTING HELP</p><h2>A good fault report saves time.</h2><p class="lead">Keep the serial number, configuration, software version and operating log with the equipment record. Describe the sequence leading to the fault and include relevant images.</p>'+faq([('Is on-site overseas repair included?','Only if included in a confirmed service agreement. Discuss the location, partner capability, scope and cost before purchase.'),('Who provides the warranty?','The named warranty provider and terms must appear in the commercial agreement. Manufacturer support and the sales partner’s duties should be stated separately.')])+'</section>'+cta()
write('/support/','Inspection ROV Training, Spare Parts & Support','Plan operator training, fault reporting, manufacturer escalation, spare parts and warranty responsibilities.',support)

auth='<p>Manufacturer authorization has been verified for the scope stated in the commercial documents.</p>' if C['authorization_verified'] else '<p>Distribution scope, product availability and manufacturer support arrangements are confirmed for each project in the written proposal.</p>'
about=intro('OUR APPROACH','Your application.<br>The complete equipment decision.','A focused equipment-selection and manufacturer-coordination approach for underwater infrastructure tasks.')
about+=f'<section class="wrap section narrow"><h2>PanPan Marine, a PanPanTech brand.</h2><p>Operated by {COMPANY}, PanPan Marine focuses on underwater equipment selection and manufacturer coordination for international infrastructure projects.</p><p>Discuss your application with our team at <a href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a>.</p></section>'
about+='<section class="wrap section two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">'+B+'</p><h2>Start with the operating conditions.</h2><p>Our site connects specific underwater tasks with the relevant Boya Gongdao equipment. It is designed to help inspection contractors and infrastructure teams define the configuration, evidence and support arrangements needed for a purchase decision.</p><p>Inspection, tunnel access, contact cleaning and sediment removal are distinct applications. Each deserves a task-specific assessment.</p></div><div class="proof-panel"><h3>Three roles to identify</h3><p><strong>Manufacturer:</strong> the producer of the equipment and source of product information.</p><p><strong>Seller:</strong> the legal entity named in the quotation and purchase agreement.</p><p><strong>Support provider:</strong> the party responsible for each agreed technical and warranty obligation.</p></div></section>'
about+='<section class="section band"><div class="wrap two-col"><div><p class="eyebrow">MANUFACTURER RELATIONSHIP</p><h2>Boya Gongdao / ROBOOCEAN.</h2><p>The product information and imagery on this site come from the supplied manufacturer brochures and official product pages. Manufacturer facilities, projects and credentials are attributed to the manufacturer.</p>'+auth+link('https://www.boyagongdao.com/','Visit the manufacturer’s website','text-link')+'</div><div>'+section_list('Review as part of supplier due diligence',['Legal seller and contractual relationship','Product and territory scope of any authorization','Quotation, payment and delivery responsibilities','Warranty, spares and technical escalation','Applicable product documents for the supplied version'])+'</div></div></section>'+cta()
write('/about/','About & Manufacturer Relationship','Understand the equipment-selection approach, manufacturer relationship and commercial responsibilities.',about)

RESOURCES=[('rov-camera-vs-sonar','Camera vs sonar for underwater inspection','Choose the sensing approach around visibility, the inspection question and required outputs.'),('tunnel-inspection-project-checklist','Underwater tunnel inspection planning checklist','Collect the geometry, flow, access, sensing and recovery information needed for a useful technical review.')]
write('/resources/','Inspection ROV Resources & Procurement Guides','Practical guides to underwater sensing and tunnel-inspection project planning.',intro('FIELD NOTES / PROCUREMENT GUIDES','Better questions.<br>Better system decisions.','Practical information to help prepare an underwater inspection brief.')+'<section class="wrap section"><div class="resource-grid">'+''.join(f'<a class="resource-card" href="/resources/{s}/"><span class="eyebrow">TECHNICAL GUIDE / 0{i}</span><h2>{t}</h2><p>{d}</p><span class="text-link">Read the guide</span></a>' for i,(s,t,d) in enumerate(RESOURCES,1))+'</div><p class="related-link"><a class="text-link" href="/blog/">Explore the blog and buying guides</a></p></section>'+cta())
camera=intro('TECHNICAL GUIDE / SENSING','Camera vs sonar for underwater inspection','The right comparison starts with the inspection question, not the sensor name.')
camera+='''<section class="wrap section article-grid"><aside class="article-aside"><h3>Prepare these inputs</h3><ul><li>Visibility and suspended material</li><li>Target size and inspection distance</li><li>Required detection and measurement</li><li>Position and reporting references</li></ul><a class="text-link" href="/solutions/industrial-underwater-inspection/">Industrial inspection guide</a></aside><div class="article-body"><section><h2>What a camera contributes</h2><p>Optical video can show recognizable surface detail, markings and material appearance when light and water clarity allow. Lighting position, suspended particles, standoff distance and camera control affect what the operator can interpret.</p><p>A sharp image does not automatically provide scaled dimensions. Measurement needs an appropriate reference or calibrated method.</p></section><section><h2>What imaging sonar contributes</h2><p>Sonar uses acoustic information and can be useful for navigation and feature recognition where optical visibility is poor. Interpretation depends on the sonar type, frequency, geometry and target.</p><p>Imaging, profiling and bathymetric sonar serve different purposes. An optional sonar interface is not proof that a particular sensor or reporting workflow has been integrated.</p></section><section><h2>Why a combined package may be appropriate</h2><p>Sonar may help the operator approach or find a target; the camera may then provide local visual detail. Confirm that both data streams can be recorded, referenced and interpreted for the actual defect or condition.</p></section><section><h2>Ask for task-relevant samples</h2><p>Request footage and acoustic data from comparable visibility, geometry and target conditions. Agree what must be detected, how it will be located and what counts as acceptable evidence.</p></section></div></section>'''
camera+='<section class="section band"><div class="wrap table-scroll"><table><caption>Questions for the sensing review</caption><thead><tr><th>Requirement</th><th>Optical review</th><th>Acoustic review</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Surface appearance</th><td>Visibility, lighting and usable standoff</td><td>Whether the target has a relevant acoustic signature</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Navigation</th><td>Available scene detail</td><td>Field of view, range and feature recognition</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Measurement</th><td>Scale reference or calibrated method</td><td>Sensor type, geometry and expected uncertainty</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Reporting</th><td>Video, stills and annotations</td><td>Recorded formats and location reference</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>'+cta()
write('/resources/rov-camera-vs-sonar/',RESOURCES[0][1],RESOURCES[0][2],camera)
checklist=intro('PROJECT GUIDE / TUNNELS',RESOURCES[1][1],RESOURCES[1][2])
checklist+='<section class="wrap section article-grid"><aside class="article-aside"><h3>Use this before quotation</h3><p>Unknown values are useful to identify. Mark them as unknown rather than filling them with assumptions.</p>'+link('/assets/tunnel-project-checklist.txt','Download checklist','button secondary')+'</aside><div class="article-body">'
checkrows=[('Route & geometry',['Total intended inspection length','Cross-sections, gradient and elevation profile','Bends, transitions, constrictions and known obstructions']),('Water & operating conditions',['Depth, flow range and expected visibility','Sediment and debris conditions','Isolation, shutdown and site permit requirements']),('Access & field logistics',['Entry opening and launch/recovery area','Lifting, reel location and available power','Staffing, communications and emergency access']),('Inspection & evidence',['Defects or condition to be assessed','Coverage and sensor requirements','Position reference, data formats and acceptance criteria']),('Failure & recovery',['Response to snagging or lost communication','Retrieval equipment and contact points','Exit conditions and site owner responsibilities'])]
for i,(t,ls) in enumerate(checkrows,1): checklist+='<section><span class="number">0'+str(i)+'</span>'+section_list(t,ls)+'</section>'
checklist+='</div></section>'+cta()
write('/resources/tunnel-inspection-project-checklist/',RESOURCES[1][1],RESOURCES[1][2],checklist)
(DIST/'assets/tunnel-project-checklist.txt').write_text('UNDERWATER TUNNEL INSPECTION — PROJECT CHECKLIST\n\n'+'\n\n'.join(t+'\n'+'\n'.join('[ ] '+i for i in ls) for t,ls in checkrows)+'\n\nMark unknown information explicitly. Review the complete system and recovery plan before purchase.\n',encoding='utf-8')

email=C.get('contact_email','')
form_note='Send the brief below and our team will review it and reply by email.'
form=intro('PROJECT CONSULTATION','Start with your site.','A short brief helps identify the right platform, configuration and technical questions.')
form+=f'''<section class="wrap section form-layout"><div><h2>Tell us what needs<br>to be done.</h2><p>Email <a class="text-link contact-email" href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a>, or prepare a structured brief below.</p><p>{form_note}</p><ol class="brief-steps"><li>Describe the task and site.</li><li>Identify key conditions and unknowns.</li><li>Send it to our team for review.</li></ol><div class="note">Do not include passwords, confidential drawings or sensitive operational information in this initial brief.</div></div><form id="proposal-form" data-email="{esc(email,quote=True)}"><div class="form-grid"><label>Your name<input name="name" autocomplete="name" required maxlength="100"></label><label>Work email<input name="email" type="email" autocomplete="email" required maxlength="254"></label><label>Company<input name="company" autocomplete="organization" required maxlength="150"></label><label>Country<input name="country" autocomplete="country-name" required maxlength="100"></label><label>Application<select name="task"><option value="">Select the task</option><option value="inspection">Industrial inspection</option><option value="tunnel">Tunnel inspection</option><option value="cleaning">Submerged cleaning</option><option value="dredging">Sump dredging</option><option value="surface">Surface cleaning</option><option value="other">Other / help me choose</option></select></label><label>Platform of interest<select name="model"><option value="">Help me select</option>{''.join('<option value="'+p['id']+'">'+p['name']+'</option>' for p in ORDERED)}<option value="tools">Tools &amp; accessories</option></select></label><label class="full">Task and required result<textarea name="description" rows="5" required maxlength="4000" placeholder="Structure, problem, required coverage or cleaning result..."></textarea></label></div><details class="optional-fields"><summary>Add site details (optional)</summary><div class="form-grid"><label>Working depth<input name="depth" maxlength="100" placeholder="e.g. 40 m / unknown"></label><label>Route or working area<input name="extent" maxlength="150" placeholder="Length, dimensions or access"></label><label>Current & visibility<input name="conditions" maxlength="250"></label><label>Expected procurement timing<input name="timing" maxlength="100"></label></div></details><label class="consent"><input type="checkbox" name="consent" required> <span>I understand how this brief is handled as described in the <a href="/privacy/">privacy notice</a>.</span></label><button class="button" type="submit">Send project brief</button><p id="form-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p><div id="brief-result" hidden><h3>Your project brief</h3><p>If online sending is unavailable, download the brief or open an email draft to {EMAIL}.</p><pre id="brief-preview"></pre><div class="actions"><button class="button" type="button" id="download-brief">Download brief</button><button class="button secondary" type="button" id="email-brief">Open email draft</button></div><p class="meta">An email draft is only delivered after you press Send in your mail application.</p></div></form></section>'''
write('/request-a-proposal/','Request a Technical Proposal','Prepare a project brief for underwater equipment selection, configuration and a technical quotation.',form)
write('/thank-you/','Your Project Brief: Next Steps','Next steps after sending an underwater equipment project brief to PanPan Marine.',intro('PROJECT BRIEF / NEXT STEPS','Thank you. Your brief has been sent.','Our team will review the task and site information and reply to the email address you provided.')+'<section class="wrap section narrow"><h2>What happens next.</h2><p>We may ask follow-up questions about the site, access and required result. Share drawings or sample data through the agreed channel once the appropriate technical contact is confirmed.</p><h3>What the technical review should resolve</h3><ul><li>Whether the task is compatible with the proposed platform</li><li>Which sensors, tools and support equipment are needed</li><li>What evidence or test demonstrates performance</li><li>Who quotes, delivers, trains and supports the system</li></ul>'+button('Return to the project brief','/request-a-proposal/')+'</section>',True)

privacy=intro('WEBSITE INFORMATION','Privacy notice','How this website handles your information. Effective 11 October 2026.')
privacy+=f'<section class="wrap section narrow"><h2>Website operator</h2><p>{COMPANY} operates PanPan Marine. For enquiries about this website or information you send us, contact <a href="mailto:{EMAIL}">{EMAIL}</a>.</p></section>'
privacy+='''<section class="wrap section narrow"><h2>Project-brief form</h2><p>When you press Send, the details you enter are transmitted to the enquiry system operated by Guangzhou PanPanTech Co., Ltd. and recorded in our internal sales tools so that our team can review your request and reply. The site does not store your form contents in browser storage.</p><p>If online sending is unavailable, the form offers a download or an email draft instead. An email draft is only sent if you press Send in your mail application; your email provider’s privacy terms apply to that transmission.</p><h2>Hosting and external services</h2><p>The hosting service may process connection information needed to deliver and secure the website. No marketing analytics, advertising pixels or optional tracking cookies have been added by this site. External links lead to services with their own privacy practices.</p><h2>Downloads</h2><p>Downloaded briefs remain on your device. Delete them when no longer needed and avoid including confidential information in an initial inquiry.</p><h2>Business contact and review</h2><p>Business enquiries you choose to email to us are used to review your request and correspond with you. Contact us using the email above with questions about information you have provided. The quotation identifies the legal seller and agreed commercial responsibilities. This notice describes the current enquiry workflow.</p></section>'''
write('/privacy/','Privacy & Cookies','Privacy information for the project-brief form, enquiry handling and website hosting.',privacy,True)
terms=intro('WEBSITE INFORMATION','Website terms','Technical information supports an initial assessment. Purchase obligations belong in the agreed contract.')
terms+='''<section class="wrap section narrow"><h2>Information and configuration</h2><p>Product figures come from supplied manufacturer brochures and official pages. They may refer to different versions or configurations. Confirm current specifications, test conditions, standard items, options and custom work in a written quotation.</p><h2>Suitability and operating conditions</h2><p>A rated depth, payload or maximum range is not a promise of successful operation in every environment. The site owner, operator and supplier should agree a task-specific plan, safe operating limits and recovery arrangements.</p><h2>Manufacturer references</h2><p>Projects described as manufacturer references are attributed to the manufacturer in China. They do not represent projects delivered by this website’s brand or evidence of performance in an untested application.</p><h2>Commercial commitments</h2><p>Prices, delivery, acceptance, payment, warranty, training and support are established in the written agreement with the named seller. Preparing a project brief does not place an order or create an accepted quotation.</p><h2>Names and materials</h2><p>Manufacturer names, product names and imagery belong to their respective holders. Source attribution does not establish an exclusive distribution arrangement or authorization. Commercial reuse of manufacturer assets and authorized-status wording requires the relevant permissions.</p></section>'''
write('/terms/','Website Terms','Technical information, manufacturer attribution and commercial terms for equipment selection.',terms,True)

